%% Platform organization, domain, and lifecycle administration
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Operator as Platform admin
    participant Web as Platform admin web
    participant API as Platform API
    participant Guard as Platform auth/permission guards
    participant Org as Organization/domain service
    participant DB as Control-plane PostgreSQL
    participant Cache as Tenant host cache
    participant Audit as Platform audit

    Operator->>Web: Open organization console
    Web->>API: GET /platform/organizations/:id
    API->>Guard: Validate platform realm and organization permission
    Guard->>Org: Load organization, domains, registry, subscription
    Org->>DB: Read control-plane metadata
    DB-->>Org: Status and domain inventory
    Org-->>API: Status and domain inventory
    API-->>Web: Status and domain inventory

    Operator->>Web: Add custom domain or reserve platform subdomain
    Web->>API: POST domain configuration
    API->>Guard: Check domain entitlement and platform permission
    Guard->>Org: Normalize and validate hostname
    Org->>DB: Persist pending domain mapping
    Org->>Audit: Record domain mutation
    Org->>Cache: Invalidate affected host mapping
    API-->>Web: Verification instructions or active domain

    opt Custom domain verification
        Operator->>Web: Submit DNS verification token
        Web->>API: POST domain verify
        API->>Org: Confirm token and domain ownership
        Org->>DB: Mark domain ACTIVE after ownership proof
        Org->>Cache: Invalidate negative cache
    end

    Operator->>Web: Select primary, disable domain, or change status
    Web->>API: Protected platform mutation
    API->>Guard: Check explicit permission
    Guard->>Org: Apply allowed transition
    Org->>DB: Persist transition and audit metadata
    Org->>Cache: Invalidate host resolution entries
    API-->>Web: Sanitized operation result

    Note over Guard,Org: Operator organization IDs target control-plane records; they do not bypass tenant authorization.
    Note over Cache,Audit: Every routing-affecting change invalidates cache and leaves an audit trail.
